From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 01:19:40 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] docs: neutralise internal governance vocabulary; explain the
 work-unit ids instead

A publication readiness pass found organisational vocabulary in tracked files - decisions
attributed to internal roles rather than stated as project policy. It reads as unexplained
jargon to anyone outside this organisation and it exposes internal structure for no benefit.
Eleven occurrences across six files are rewritten to state the decision, not the decider. No
technical content changed: every default, measurement and caveat is identical.

The 'lane-NNN' work-unit ids are deliberately KEPT, and README now explains why: each one ties
a change to the block of work that produced it, the machine it was measured on, and the file
holding the raw numbers. Scrubbing them would cost the traceability that makes the measured
claims checkable, which is the opposite of the point. They are documented as a ticket
reference would be, alongside the Taken-from: and Measured-effect: trailer conventions.

Note: 'HQ' still appears in src/models/minimax-m3.cpp as an upstream variable name for the
head-query dimension. That is upstream code and unrelated; it is left alone.

Origin: ArifiLabs lane-110D, public-release bar
Measured-effect: documentation only; no engine behaviour changed.
